#
# Nxp SPi protocol (SPI) devices
#

menuconfig NFC_P61_DEVICES
    bool "Nxp SPi protocol driver (SPI) devices"
    default n
    ---help---
      You'll have to say Y if your computer contains an SPI device that
      you want to use under Linux.

      You can say N here if you don't have any SPI connected to your computer.

if NFC_P61_DEVICES 

config P61_NFC_SPI
    tristate "PN61 NFC driver"
    default n
    ---help---
      Say yes if you want SPI protocol driver.
      This is for spi connected version. If unsure, say N here.

      To compile this driver as a module, choose m here. The module will
      be called 6p1.


endif # NFC_P61_DEVICES
